A||||6||Greg Piet||I Hate oil leaks||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||04-04-2000||02:05 PM||||GRRRR  I just want to gripe.<BR>I have an oil leak which I thought was at the harmonic balancer/crankshaft.  I replaced the seal, but it appears I still have the leak!<BR>ARGH!<BR>Now I have to power wash the motor over there real good again and try to find the frigging leak again!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||04-04-2000||03:33 PM||||If it's a v6, have you checked the distributor o-ring?  That's where 99% of the oil leaks on the 6 come from.. mine's leaking there.  The o-ring is still available from the dealer.. don't know the p/n but it costs around $1.30.  Valve covers are another place to check.. good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||04-04-2000||03:43 PM||||Yeah I got that one fixed already...   that one is on the other side of the motor.<P>I also had a speedo sensor leak which required yet another o ring.<BR>Oh well!||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-04-2000||06:27 PM||||the balancer's not grooved around the seal area is it? If it is, even a little you'll likely need a sleeve for the balancer.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroshop||04-04-2000||07:49 PM||||One other place that I have found a leak on that side of the motor is the oil sender will sometimes leak right thru the top of it. I have had to replace several oil senders for this reason. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||04-05-2000||02:50 PM||||oil sender?   Do you mean the oil pressure sensor pipe?  ill have to look a that.  I didnt notice any grooves on the balancer, but i guess ill have to look closer at it if that appears to be the leaking area after further inspection!<BR>Thanks for the ideas!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||04-05-2000||04:00 PM||||One more idea that may or may not apply to the V6.<P>On the 4 (84 anyhow), the timing gear cover does not have any alignment pins. Is is possible (really quite easy) to have the cover installed so the seal is off center of the crankshaft. This of course can cause even a brand new seal to leak.||||reg||3
